By Rotation, launched October 2019, operates a peer-to-peer fashion rental app enabling individuals to rent and lend designer pieces directly. Users monetize unused wardrobe items while accessing curated designer collections affordably. The model proves significantly more sustainable than linear retail: peer-sourced inventory produces 42% less CO2 throughout product lifecycles versus inventory-based rental. P2P platforms source from individual 'lenders' rather than manufacturers, reducing production pressure and increasing utilization rates. By Rotation exemplifies how community-driven platforms lower transaction friction and environmental overhead, enabling circular consumption through trusted networks. The model empowers users as economic agents in circular systems while building cultural acceptance of fashion as access rather than ownership.